**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests`
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests`, `BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests`

**How to implement.** The Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models become axis data, so no model lowers to the evaluated case (.spec-md §3.1). (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: `ForouhiBloomerLaw` (`nInf`, `a`, `b`, `c`, `bandGap`, `abscissa`) and `BrendelBormannLaw` (`plasmaFrequency`, `intrabandStrength`, `intrabandDamping`, then `strength`, `resonance`, `damping` and `broadening` as `float list`, then `abscissa`), marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier("...")>]`. Each has a `complexIndex` whose body is its arm of `baseIndex` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:518-538`) moved verbatim over `this.abscissa.abscissaAt w`. Weideman's Faddeeva series (`faddeevaTermCount`, `FaddeevaSeries`, `faddeevaSeries` and `faddeeva`, `:437-483`) moves into `Dispersion.fs` beside `BrendelBormannLaw`, stays private there, and is deleted from the Domain. `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `ForouhiBloomerAxis of ForouhiBloomerLaw` and `BrendelBormannAxis of BrendelBormannLaw`, with `complexIndex`, `Equals` and `GetHashCode` arms as in step 5. (2) `DispersionModels.fs`: `ForouhiBloomerCoefficients.toForouhiBloomerLaw` and `BrendelBormannCoefficients.toBrendelBormannLaw`, built as step 5's members are. `baseIndex`'s two arms answer the law's index. `toEpsAxis` lowers both models to their cases, so its `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate` line (`:766-769`) is gone and every model lowers to data. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm answers `[]` for both cases. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` maps both cases to `DiscreteKey "Evaluated (transcendental)"`, and `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats both as data that is not editable term data. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `The Forouhi-Bloomer law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap` and `The Brendel-Bormann law reproduces its reference index`. They use the `forouhiBloomerASi` and `brendelBormannGold` sets (`DispersionModelsTests.fs:403-430`) over the electron-volt abscissa, at 300, 450, 600, 900 and 2000 nm, exact against G17 literals recorded from the pre-move `DispersionModel.evaluate`. Three arms that matched `EpsAxisEvaluated _` follow the law cases: `AC-B6 ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`DispersionModelsTests.fs:534-552`); `step 015: a transcendental dispersive segment derives and evaluates without rejection` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs:321-340`), which also asserts `Assert.False(c.isEditable)`, pinning the unchanged view-only behaviour; and `ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann are pickable and lower to the evaluated segment` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs:305-317`). Their other assertions are unchanged, and their comments no longer name `EpsAxisEvaluated`.

**Acceptance.** After the two laws land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data` (red since step 6), with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B6 reference facts unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the two new law facts equal to their literals; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.
